-- title:
--   Coefficient certificates for Klein's edge form under U, part 1
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $\alpha,\beta,s\in K$ satisfy the four relations $\alpha\beta=-s$, $2\alpha^{2}=-5-s$, $2\beta^{2}=s-5$ and $s^{2}=5$. Then ten explicit polynomial identities hold simultaneously. Each identity equates a fixed integer-coefficient linear combination of monomials $\alpha^{a}\beta^{b}$ with $a+b=30$ to a constant of $K$: the first identity, with the combination $\beta^{30}+522\,\alpha^{5}\beta^{25}-10005\,\alpha^{10}\beta^{20}-10005\,\alpha^{20}\beta^{10}-522\,\alpha^{25}\beta^{5}+\alpha^{30}$, has right-hand side $30517578125=5^{15}$; the sixth, whose combination begins $522\,\beta^{30}-65250\,\alpha^{2}\beta^{28}+\cdots$ and ends $+522\,\alpha^{30}$, has right-hand side $-15930175781250=-522\cdot 5^{15}$; the remaining eight combinations, listed in full in the statement with coefficients ranging up to magnitude about $3.4\cdot 10^{10}$, are all equal to $0$. No further hypothesis on $\alpha,\beta,s$ or on $K$ is imposed; in particular the assertion is a purely algebraic consequence of the four displayed relations.
--
--   This is the first of three blocks of coefficient certificates (here the coefficients of $u^{k}$ for the ten lowest values of $k$) expressing the covariance of Klein's binary edge form of degree $30$ under the half-turn $U=\tfrac1s\begin{pmatrix}-\alpha&\beta\\ \beta&\alpha\end{pmatrix}$ of the binary icosahedral group, the abstract elements $\alpha,\beta,s$ standing for $\zeta-\zeta^{4}$, $\zeta^{2}-\zeta^{3}$ and $\sqrt5$ with $\zeta$ a primitive fifth root of unity. It is used by [`RubinSilverberg.kleinTHom_atomsU`](thm.html#RubinSilverberg.kleinTHom_atomsU) in verifying that $U$ is a symmetry of the Rubin–Silverberg datum for the family of elliptic curves with constant mod-$5$ representation.
